# LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# gofmt refuses CRLF and rewrites files on sight, so a Windows checkout with
# `core.autocrlf=true` (the default, and what the windows-latest runner uses)
# makes the whole tree look unformatted. Normalising here keeps a clone
# byte-identical across machines.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.db binary
*.exe binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.dll binary

# PowerShell scripts keep CRLF (Windows PowerShell 5.1 continuity semantics).
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
